SECTION | KEY | VALUE
----------------------------------------
# time.pdl - the pet's TIME: what the clock fires and when. Each row becomes a reminder on the pet's own livedesk clock (installed by ops/pet_clock.sh install; the clock only runs while the pet is started).
# AT | event | when | repeat | what it does           when = HH:MM of the game day (or +N<m|h|d>);  repeat = every:<n><min|hour|day|week>
# Each event is a pet_event.sh verb run for every STARTED pet (clock_event). Edit here, then Menu > Time > Reinstall schedule (or delete state/clock_root).
AT | need_tick | +1h    | every:1hour | hunger, energy and cleanliness drift (weights tick_hunger / tick_energy / tick_clean)
AT | meal_call | 08:00  | every:1day  | breakfast: a hungry pet says so, and may feed itself (self_care skill)
AT | meal_call | 12:00  | every:1day  | lunch
AT | meal_call | 18:00  | every:1day  | dinner
AT | bedtime   | 22:00  | every:1day  | sleepy: it may put itself to bed (self_care)
AT | wake      | 06:00  | every:1day  | morning: some energy back, a greeting
AT | phase_dawn  | 06:00  | every:1day  | sunrise: outdoor views turn orange (writes state/daylight.txt phase=dawn)
AT | phase_day   | 08:00  | every:1day  | full day
AT | phase_dusk  | 17:00  | every:1day  | sunset
AT | phase_night | 19:00  | every:1day  | night: moon, stars, dark water, no birds
AT | day_tick  | 00:00  | every:1day  | the day ends: skill MP refills, grade check, evolution
# speeds the Time menu offers (lc_clock rates, MEASURED 2026-10-09 per real second): cent = 100 game hours (testing only), sec = 1 game hour (a day in 24 s), min = 1 game minute (a day in 24 min, the default), hour = real time, day = nearly frozen
SPEED | cent
SPEED | sec
SPEED | min
SPEED | hour
